From a1b5a38290485969c0be03c34feed9daf3124192 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:42:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(stub): add stub VM type for hypervisor-free testing

Add an experimental `stub` VM type that follows the normal VM lifecycle and
state machine, creates real taps, appears in `vm info`, and offers the miniccc
backchannel over a unix socket, but runs no QEMU process and no container, so
that minimega and orchestrators such as phenix can be tested end to end on CI
hosts without a hypervisor. Stub VMs reuse ContainerConfig, so `vm config init`
optionally names a host process that is started as a stand-in guest with
MM_STUB_* environment variables, and `vm config filesystem` is ignored. Add
unit tests, stub_lifecycle and stub_info minitests, and documentation.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
